{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And this is the law of the meal-offering.</b> It has already been stated in the section ויקרא, 'When a soul brings a meal-offering' (Leviticus 2:1), but it is mentioned here on account of four commandments added to it. <b>The first</b>, that it be eaten unleavened, as it says מצות תאכל — 'unleavened you shall eat it.' <b>The second</b>, that it be eaten in the court of the Tent of Meeting, as it says בחצר אהל מועד יאכלוה — 'in the court of the Tent of Meeting they shall eat it.' <b>The third</b>, that every male among the sons of Aharon eat it. <b>The fourth</b>, that it consecrate everything that touches it: if minor holy things or unconsecrated things touch it, they become consecrated to be like it — so if it was disqualified they become disqualified, and if it was fit it is eaten according to the stringency of the meal-offering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:16.485144364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}